/**
 * TRIPLE-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER: LIVING WITH IT, CARE AND DECISIONS (UK and NHS focus). Facts checked 2026-09-24.
 *
 * The patient side of the TNBC record, to the gallbladder standard (./gallbladder-living.ts): eleven decision rows
 * the decisions page turns into sections (chemotherapy before or after surgery; adding pembrolizumab and what PD-L1
 * means here; residual disease and the capecitabine or olaparib choice; mastectomy or breast-conserving surgery and
 * when to reconstruct; radiotherapy schedules; fertility preservation; genetic testing and the family; first treatment
 * for metastatic disease and the tests that decide it; antibody-drug conjugates and their side effects; brain
 * metastases; a trial or standard treatment), the hand-written question set the appointment sheet, prep pack and
 * decision pages read (exported as `tnbcQuestions`, wired in src/data/questions.ts), and living-with material
 * attached as sourced notes and links to the side-effect and procedure records other files own (neuropathy, hair
 * loss and scalp cooling, immune-related side effects, neutropenia and infection, ADC diarrhoea and eye care,
 * fatigue, menopause after chemotherapy, lymphoedema, body image and reconstruction, work and money).
 *
 * This file creates no glossary terms: the core file (./tnbc-core.ts) owns them. Drafts for the eight terms this material
 * wants are exported as `tnbcLivingTermDrafts` and registered from the core file verbatim; the ids they use are listed
 * in the drafts. Trials are owned by the treatment file (./tnbc-treatment.ts), which now carries CREATE-X.
 *
 * Every medical statement points at an NHS, Macmillan, Cancer Research UK, Breast Cancer Now, Maggie's or Triple
 * Negative Breast Cancer Foundation page, a NICE guideline or appraisal, or a paper read through Europe PMC. Nothing
 * here is advice; the pages say so the way the site's other living-with material does. UK spelling, plain English.
 *
 * The cancer record itself (`tnbc`) lives in src/data/cancers.ts; if it is renamed, change TNBC_CANCER_ID and the
 * questions key together. The checklist for the first 60 days is in src/data/first-60-days-checklists.ts, the red
 * cards in src/data/red-flags.ts (cancerIds: ["tnbc"]) and the decision aid in src/data/decision-tools/tnbc-after-chemotherapy.ts.
 */
